.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Implements the Grøstl-256 and Grøstl-512 hashing functions as part of the \fBSystemEx\fP low-level cryptographic subsystem\&. This class provides a fully self-contained, allocation-free, deterministic hash engine based on the original Grøstl specification (SHA-3 finalist)\&. 

The implementation is designed for systems programming scenarios where predictable behavior, portability, and runtime independence are required\&. All operations are performed using fixed-size buffers, explicit state transformations, and constant-time primitives where applicable\&.

.PP
GroestlHash exposes two public hashing interfaces: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCompute\fP — Produces a 32-bit hash derived from the full Grøstl-256 digest\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBComputeLong\fP — Produces a 64-bit hash derived from the full Grøstl-512 digest\&. 
.PP

.PP
Both variants support endian-aware extraction and optional seed mixing, enabling integration into heterogeneous environments, custom keying schemes, and internal hashing pipelines\&.

.PP
This class is intended for: 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
Deterministic hashing inside low-level frameworks 
.IP "\(bu" 2
Internal key generation and seeding mechanisms 
.IP "\(bu" 2
Data integrity checks and non-cryptographic fingerprinting 
.IP "\(bu" 2
Embedded or isolated verification modules 
.PP

