.SS "\fBHash32\fP SystemEx\&.Hash\&.GrøstlHash\&.Compute (FixedVector< byte > input, uint seed)"

.PP
Computes a 32-bit hash value based on the Grøstl-256 digest for the specified input buffer, with optional seed mixing and endian-aware extraction\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP The input byte sequence to be hashed\&. This is treated as an opaque binary buffer and processed according to the Grøstl-256 specification, including padding and compression\&. The full 256-bit digest is computed internally and then reduced to a 32-bit value\&. 
.br
\fIseed\fP An optional 21-bit seed value that is XOR-mixed into the final hash result\&. This allows callers to derive distinct hash domains, build keyed hash variants, or introduce additional application-specific entropy without altering the core Grøstl-256 computation\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fBHash32\fP instance containing the 32-bit hash value derived from the Grøstl-256 digest of \fIinput\fP , after endian-aware extraction and XOR-mixing with \fIseed\fP \&. 
.RE
.PP

